        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Lebanon leaders accuse Israel of war crime after journalist killed Middle East Issued on: 23/04/2026 - 20:39 Lebanon's president and prime minister accused Israel on Thursday of a war crime, after an airstrike killed a Lebanese journalist in the country's south, where Israeli forces occupy several areas. Rescuers and the reporter's employer on Wednesday confirmed the death of Amal Khalil, a 42-year-old journalist who worked for the Lebanese daily Al-Akbar. Israel defense minister says awaiting US green light to 'return Iran to Stone Age' 23/04/2026 Middle East Iran flaunts its grip over the Strait of Hormuz with commandos storming cargo ship 23/04/2026 Middle East Trump orders Iran mine-layers sunk, as Iran tolls tankers 23/04/2026 Middle East 'The future is peace': A story of brotherhood across a divided land 23/04/2026 Middle East EU 'must' shift to renewables to end fossil fuel 'blackmail from war-driving authoritarian regimes' 23/04/2026 Middle East Gulf allies have requested financial support, US Treasury Secretary says 22/04/2026 Middle East 'Right now both sides are testing each other', analyst says as Iran truce extended 22/04/2026 Middle East French soldier dies of wounds after attack on UN force in Lebanon 22/04/2026 Middle East Three ships targeted in Hormuz, Iran seizes two 22/04/2026 Middle East"
